.TH RADIOWARE\-SOURCE 1 "July 2026" "radioware\-source 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
radioware\-source \- Radioware audio source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B radioware\-source
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads f32le PCM audio from a UDP socket, encodes it with Opus, and streams the
result to an output UDP socket.
.PP
Settings are resolved by layering, from lowest to highest precedence: built\-in
defaults, the TOML configuration file, \fBRADIOWARE_*\fR environment variables,
and finally the command\-line flags described below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to the TOML configuration file (default: radioware.toml).
.TP
.BR \-\-input\-bind " " \fIHOST:PORT\fR
Address the input UDP socket binds to.
.TP
.BR \-\-input\-samplerate " " \fIHZ\fR
Sample rate, in Hz, of the incoming f32le PCM.
.TP
.BR \-\-channels " " \fIN\fR
Number of interleaved audio channels in the input stream.
.TP
.BR \-\-frame\-duration " " \fIMS\fR
Codec frame duration, in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR \-\-output\-bind " " \fIHOST:PORT\fR
Address the output UDP socket binds to locally.
.TP
.BR \-\-output\-host " " \fIHOST:PORT\fR
Destination the encoded audio is sent to.
.TP
.BR \-\-output\-samplerate " " \fIHZ\fR
Output sample rate, in Hz.
.TP
.BR \-\-output\-bitrate " " \fIBPS\fR
Target Opus bitrate, in bits per second.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/radioware/source.toml
System\-wide configuration file installed by the package.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOG_LEVEL
Log verbosity: one of \fBerror\fR, \fBwarn\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBdebug\fR or
\fBtrace\fR (default: warn).
.TP
.B RADIOWARE_*
Any configuration key can be set through an environment variable of the same
name with a \fBRADIOWARE_\fR prefix, e.g. \fBRADIOWARE_INPUT_BIND\fR.
